 ],
 "note": "Black car with the neon STAR CHIP scheme. No near side-on photo of the left side: positions measured on the Getty / LAT photo 'Brands Hatch 26 August 1991, Dave Brodie' (2201200916, right side, mirrored and warped onto the model by the wheel centres and window corners); the left side is confirmed by the other LAT photo of that day (2201200818, front three-quarter, nose left: same number board, STAR CHIP on the front wing, lattice on the rear door, Brodie on the rear window) and the Thruxton TV graphic drawings. Same 4-door Sapphire shell as Gravett's car. Uncertain: the lattice and orange loops are drawn as a regular pattern (the real graphic is hand-drawn and irregular); star sizes and the exact stripe order on the bumpers are approximate; small stickers (Bilstein, Hoosier, the round logo) are partly unreadable. Wheels: dark centres with a polished lip, from on-track photos only (no photo of the car standing still)."
}